-- The public-sector framework agreements' root (MMS-538; the client,
-- 2026-11-15: the framework agreements are a family of their own): the
-- agreements of the corpus's agreements/framework family that speak to an
-- item of the shared vocabulary (l4/lib/vocabulary.l4), each registered once
-- as an instrument (it describes itself in its own file), and what each
-- claims for a case. The agreements' root (l4/lib/agreements-root.l4)
-- imports it beside the other families' roots and rules among all their
-- agreements by one rule, §19 then §23 (MMS-686); precedence between
-- collections is left to l4/lib/precedence.l4.
--
-- It imports the whole family (its import block is written by
-- tools/roots.py --write-agreement-imports). No framework agreement answers
-- an item of the vocabulary yet: none describes itself as an instrument or
-- has an `<item> according to <agreement>` answer, so this root includes
-- none and claims nothing. The first that does is registered here.

